{%- comment -%}
  Self-hosted, latin-subset webfonts — the original Pinemoor type system.

  Clash Grotesk sets every heading, Satoshi sets body copy, and Tenor Sans is
  used for one thing only: the Pinemoor wordmark, so the header matches the
  lettering on the bottle label. All are variable fonts, so a single file covers
  every weight the theme uses.

  Serving them as theme assets keeps type on a connection the page already has
  open — no third-party font origins, nothing render-blocking.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'pm-satoshi.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'pm-clash-grotesk.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
<style>
@font-face{font-family:'Satoshi';src:url('{{ 'pm-satoshi.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');font-weight:300 900;font-style:normal;font-display:swap;}
@font-face{font-family:'Clash Grotesk';src:url('{{ 'pm-clash-grotesk.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');font-weight:200 700;font-style:normal;font-display:swap;}
@font-face{font-family:'Tenor Sans';src:url('{{ 'pm-tenor-sans-400.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-display:swap;}
@font-face{font-family:'Outfit';src:url('{{ 'pm-outfit.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');font-weight:100 900;font-style:normal;font-display:swap;}
</style>
